  "title": ":compass: Public Launch Post",
  "summary": "LinkedIn Post If you’re building AI models and working with PyTorch, GPU kernels, or performance tuning… you probably know the pain of profiling. Running a trace on a remote GPU… Downloading 200MB+ files… Opening Nsight or Perfetto locally… Still not knowing which line of code triggered the slowdown. Then branching your code to sprinkle profiling markers, re-running everything, and waiting 10–30 minutes for each iteration. The whole workflow feels like wading through butter. We’ve felt this...",
